The best way to iterate a `HashMap` in NAME_1 is to use the `entrySet()` method of the `HashMap` class, which returns a set view of the key-value mappings contained in the map. Then, you can iterate over the entries using a for-each loop:
```vbnet
for (Map.Entry<String, Integer> entry : map.entrySet()) {
    String key = entry.getKey();
    Integer value = entry.getValue();
    // do something with the key and value
}
```
Alternatively, you can use the `keys()` and `values()` methods of the `HashMap` class to get an iterator for the keys and values respectively, and then iterate over the iterator:
```csharp
Iterator<String> keys = map.keys();
while (keys.hasNext()) {
    String key = keys.next();
    Integer value = map.get(key);
    // do something with the key and value
}

Iterator<Integer> values = map.values();
while (values.hasNext()) {
    Integer value = values.next();
    String key = map.get(value);
    // do something with the key and value
}
```
Note that you need to check if the iterator has more elements before using its methods.

